an","metadata":{"type":"prototype-element","tag":"span","rect":{"x":17,"y":315,"width":318,"height":28},"textAlign":"left"},"width":318,"height":28,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"frame","id":"rqwL6","x":0,"y":2.5,"name":"span","context":"span","metadata":{"type":"prototype-element","tag":"span","rect":{"x":0,"y":2.5,"width":95.59,"height":23},"textAlign":"left"},"width":96,"height":23,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"text","id":"Piggq","x":0,"y":1,"name":"A3 · HELD","metadata":{"type":"prototype-text","rect":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":95.59,"height":22},"align":"left"},"fill":"#909090","content":"A3 · HELD","lineHeight":1,"fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":20,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"Jyu3N","x":290,"y":0,"name":"rack-power","context":"span","metadata":{"type":"prototype-element","tag":"span","rect":{"x":290,"y":0,"width":28,"height":28},"textAlign":"left"},"width":28,"height":28,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"frame","id":"E3pTu9","x":0,"y":0,"name":"ui-icon","context":"svg","metadata":{"type":"prototype-element","tag":"svg","rect":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":28,"height":28},"textAlign":"left"},"clip":true,"width":28,"height":28,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"path","id":"wniQn","x":0,"y":0,"name":"Navigation icon","geometry":"M12 3v9m-6.36-6.36a9 9 0 1 0 12.72 0","viewBox":[0,0,24,24],"width":28,"height":28,"stroke":"#797979","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinejoin":"round","strokeLinecap":"round"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"frame","id":"JpkzX","x":36,"y":428,"name":"effects-off-band","width":1848,"height":68,"fill":"#e0a94a24","layout":"none","children":[{"type":"rectangle","id":"YinCv","x":0,"y":0,"name":"warning-edge","fill":"$warning","width":3,"height":68},{"type":"text","id":"D184pw","x":27,"y":23,"name":"Effects off consequence","fill":"#f3f4f7","content":"Effects are off for this input: you hear it dry, and new takes record dry.","lineHeight":1,"fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"normal"},{"type":"frame","id":"G3guuP","x":1580,"y":8,"name":"turn-effects-on","width":260,"height":52,"fill":"#3b82f6","cornerRadius":8,"gap":10,"justifyContent":"center","alignItems":"center","children":[{"type":"text","id":"rmIHN","name":"Turn effects on","fill":"#ffffff","content":"Turn effects on","lineHeight":1,"fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":20,"fontWeight":"normal"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"text","id":"PcR1d","x":2200,"y":5348,"name":"c/ Effects power and new racks (#1452)","fill":"#a3adbd","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":1840,"content":"c/ Effects power and new racks (#1452, owner decisions 2026-10-23)\n\nEffects power is the chain's own switch, separate from rack activation and pedal power: Off takes every effect on this input, take, track, All tracks or output out of the sound and leaves each rack and pedal as it is. It is the segmented Effects Off | On beside Hear live (or the part picker), and the first control of the rack and effect editors' title row, so it can be turned back on from every screen that shows those effects, not only from a pedal binding.\n\nWhile it is off, the racks or pedals under it dim, and one band in the warning colour over them says what that does to the sound (an input monitors dry and new takes record dry) and carries Turn effects on. It is the only notice for this cause: no toast. Rack and pedal switches stay usable under the dim, so a sound can be prepared before the effects go back on. A source card says Effects off under its name while its chain is off, so a dry input shows before it is selected. The Stage does not mark it.\n\nAn added factory rack keeps each pedal on or off as the preset sets it (as the Looper X loads a rack), a saved sound arrives as it was saved, and a single effect arrives on. This replaces the earlier rule that every new instance starts bypassed. A new pedal fades in over the engine's 5 ms enable ramp rather than switching in at full.\n\nWhy: on build .195 both inputs' chains were saved off; the page read as on, the only way back was the foot FX mode, and racks arriving with every pedal off compounded the silence.","lineHeight":1.4,"fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":28,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"CnUFF","x":6700,"y":300,"name":"02  Effects · chains & controls","width":6320,"height":4076,"fill":"#1a1d24","cornerRadius":24,"stroke":"#48505f","strokeWidth":2,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"text","id":"byUcT","x":120,"y":62,"name":"02  Effects · chains & controls / Section title","fill":"#d5ddf5","content":"02  Effects · chains & controls","fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":68,"fontWeight":"700"},{"type":"text","id":"vGc3B","x":120,"y":160,"name":"02  Effects · chains & controls / Status","fill":"#a3adbd","content":"Current study  ·  6 screens","fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":36,"fontWeight":"normal"},{"type":"frame","id":"b1UGvn","x":120,"y":260,"name":"01 / Connected pedal editor","width":1920,"height":1152,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"text","id":"tNY3A","x":0,"y":10,"name":"Screen label / Connected pedal editor","fill":"#c9ced9","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":1920,"content":"01  Connected pedal editor","fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":32,"fontWeight":"700"},{"type":"frame","id":"o0RK7c","x":0,"y":72,"name":"FX UX 2026 / Connected pedal editor","context":"section","clip":true,"width":1920,"height":1080,"fill":"#111215","layout":"none","children":[{"type":"frame","id":"ZexJt","x":0,"y":0,"name":"topbar","context":"header","metadata":{"type":"prototype-element","tag":"header","rect":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":1920,"height":96},"textAlign":"start"},"width":1920,"height":96,"stroke":"#3d3d3d","strokeWidth":{"bottom":1},"strokeAlignment":"inner","layout":"none","children":[{"type":"frame","id":"t1StY","x":36,"y":15.5,"name":"Back","context":"Prototype control: back","metadata":{"type":"prototype-element","tag":"button","rect":{"x":36,"y":15.5,"width":64,"height":64},"textAlign":"center"},"width":64,"height":64,"cornerRadius":8,"stroke":"#515d6e","strokeWidth":1,"strokeAlignment":"inner","layout":"none"