dth":3,"strokeAlignment":"inner"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"text","id":"po4RZ","x":2200,"y":2804,"name":"c/ Implementation · slice 4c","fill":"#a3adbd","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":1840,"content":"c/ Native implementation · Pedal setup (#1026 / PR #1028)\nLayout A uses the accepted Fusion pedal body, rubber pad, grips and nameplate. The raised rear row keeps its full touch area. Track holds edit all four tracks together; fixed Stop, Undo, Clear and Bank stay dimmed and outside focus. Pedals is reachable from Settings and the Control tray. Stage closes that tray.\nSave waits for storage confirmation before activating a draft. Cancel keeps the existing setup. Failed writes restore the exact prior data; if that restoration also fails, a persistent warning and Save remain available. Unreadable explicit assignments stay inactive: “Saved assignments can’t be read. Review these replacements, then Save to enable them.” Cancel never replaces damaged data; only a confirmed Save enables the reviewed replacement.\nMode has separate Press and Hold. Record/Play and track presses retain immediate transport contact. Track Hold acts only in Tracks; Record/Play Hold also works in Mute. Arm overdub cannot cancel a pending arm or finish a capture started elsewhere. Bank Hold retains performance-recording access.\nStaged capability: this PR exposes Track controls only. Custom setup returns with its real runtime in PR #1030, together with the accepted Mode Hold → Custom default. The interim Hold → FX is not the final design. LED colors, External pedals, double-press Solo and later performance actions remain separate slices. Physical control validation still requires the appliance.","lineHeight":1.3,"fontFamily":"Arimo","fontSize":24,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"q2xSj","x":180,"y":17324,"name":"09  External pedals","width":6320,"height":6620,"fill":"#1a1d24","cornerRadius":24,"stroke":"#48505f","strokeWidth":2,"layout":"none","children":[{"type":"text","id":"WpeY3","x":12